{
  "id": "COMPOUND:18648 - PROTEIN:6138",
  "verbalization": "Nigrolineaxanthone F is implicated in targeting Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which in turn is a target of Phorone and 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol. These compounds are linked to the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Nigrolineaxanthone F may act as a modulator of the proteasome pathway, potentially through the indirect activation of the 26S proteasome by these downstream targets. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Nigrolineaxanthone F influences the proteasome's regulatory subunit 14 via a chain of enzymatic interactions, possibly by affecting the activity or stability of the SDR family member 9. This mechanism underscores the role of the SDR family in mediating the effects of Nigrolineaxanthone F on the proteasome, suggesting a broader impact on protein degradation and cellular homeostasis.",
